From 56ff5a68cf06dd3fff6130c9ef26ec98f3b5e41c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:19:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] process adoption: parse failures record rc 2; a
 foreign kill settles as killed; foreign poll/wait get the local policy; docks
 map unknown

Follow-up to PR #2376 review 5894247825 (nits 1-4; nit 5 was declined on the PR).

1. Parse failures record their status. The exit recorder pasted the command inline into
   `( ... )`, which bash parses whole before running: a syntax error (or an unterminated
   heredoc that ate the closing paren) killed the recording shell itself with status 2,
   nothing was recorded, and the adopted job settled as `unknown`. The child now `eval`s the
   shell-quoted command text, so the parse error ends only the child and the recorder writes
   its 2. `eval` parses one command at a time, as an unwrapped `bash -c` does: an unterminated
   heredoc now behaves exactly as it does unwrapped (warning, runs), and aliases defined
   earlier in the command apply to later lines (they did not inside the compound).

2. A foreign kill settles as killed. `process_manage kill` from a process that does not
   supervise the job (process_registry_foreign) returned `killed`, but the supervisor only
   saw the PID go with no recorded status and its one completion notice said "status
   unknown". The foreign kill now writes a `<log>.killed` marker (termination source) before
   signalling; the supervisor's log reader settles a marked exit as killed (-15,
   termination_source process.kill, "terminated by process.kill"), for an adopter and for a
   live spawner holding the Popen alike. A kill that leaves the root alive (survivors, scope
   stop failed) withdraws the marker, so a later natural exit is not misreported. The foreign
   poll/log/wait exit fields read the marker too. The marker also retires the log after the
   result retention, as a recorded `.exit` does (a killed job never writes one).

3. Foreign poll/wait use the local post-processing. `_handle_process` applied
   `apply_wait_poll_policy` and `with_masked_success_hint` before the foreign fallback, so a
   foreign result skipped both; they now run after it (the policy is a no-op for a session
   this registry does not hold, the masked-success hint applies).

4. Docks map `unknown`. `cli_process_dock` and the TUI `processRoster` had no mapping for the
   `unknown` (and `watcher_lost`) completion reasons, so an unrecorded exit (exit_code None)
   painted as done. Both now show an `unknown` status: `?` glyph, verdict "status unknown"
   (new `cli.dock.verdict_unknown` key in all 17 catalogs).

Proof:
- RED (tests only, source at main): 8 failures in test_process_restart_adoption_matrix.py
  (syntax_error x2, unterminated_heredoc x2, owner kill notice, masked hint, kill-marker
  retention) and test_process_dock.py (unknown status); vitest processDock "never paints a
  re-adopted job whose exit status was not recorded as done" fails.
- GREEN: both files 25+ passed; vitest processDock 3/3; tsc --noEmit, eslint, prettier clean.
- Mutants killed: dropping the reader's kill-marker branch fails the owner-kill and
  spawner-kill tests; dropping either marker withdrawal fails the withdraw tests.
- Wider: 15 importing/related files (process registry, readopt, persist, wait auto-notify,
  completion delivery, i18n, ...) 352 passed, 4 skipped.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 19 checks ok.
